{"name":"Bamboo Mat","hex":"#e5da9f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bamboo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the fast-growing grasses of the Bambusoideae subfamily, characterized by its woody, hollow, round, straight, jointed stem.","Wood of the bamboo plant as a material for building, furniture, etc."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of the wood of the bamboo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bamboo"},{"term":"mat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Matlatzinca."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat piece of coarse material used for wiping one’s feet, or as a decorative or protective floor covering.","A small flat piece of material used to protect a surface from anything hot or rough; a coaster."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bamboo","blocks":[{"text":"Bamboos are a diverse group of mostly evergreen perennial flowering plants making up the subfamily Bambusoideae of the grass family Poaceae. Giant bamboos are the largest members of the grass family, in the case of Dendrocalamus sinicus having individual stalks (culms) reaching a length of 46 meters (151 ft), up to 36 centimeters (14 in) in diameter and a weight of up to 450 kilograms (1,000 lb). It grows in tropical and subtropical regions, especially in Asia. The internodes of bamboos can also be of great length. Kinabaluchloa wrayi has internodes up to 2.5 meters (8 ft) in length, and Arthrostylidium schomburgkii has internodes up to 5 meters (16 ft) in length, exceeded in length only by papyrus. By contrast, the stalks of the tiny bamboo Raddiella vanessiae of the savannas of French Guiana measure only 10–20 millimeters (0.4–0.8 in) in length by about 2 millimeters (0.08 in) in width. The origin of the word \"bamboo\" is uncertain, but it most likely comes from the Dutch or Portuguese language, which originally borrowed it from Malay."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Bamboo_forest.jpg/330px-Bamboo_forest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bamboo","wikidata":"Q670887"},{"title":"Mat","blocks":[{"text":"A mat is a hard or soft floor covering that generally is placed on a floor or other flat surface. Mats serve a range of purposes including:"},{"items":["serving to clean items passed over it, such as a doormat, which removes dirt from the soles of shoes","protecting that which is above the mat, such as a wrestling or gymnastics mat, or an anti-vibration mat","protecting that which is beneath the mat, such as a place mat"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Welcome_doormat.JPG/330px-Welcome_doormat.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mat","wikidata":"Q1136834"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Big_Bamboo_Shoot_%28Joi_Ito%29.jpg/500px-Big_Bamboo_Shoot_%28Joi_Ito%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Big_Bamboo_Shoot_%28Joi_Ito%29.jpg/500px-Big_Bamboo_Shoot_%28Joi_Ito%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh bamboo shoot emerging from the soil. These young, tender culms of bamboo plants are also widely harvested for culinary use in Asia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABig_Bamboo_Shoot_(Joi_Ito).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/2021_Sagano_Bamboo_forest_in_Arashiyama%2C_Kyoto%2C_Japan.jpg/500px-2021_Sagano_Bamboo_forest_in_Arashiyama%2C_Kyoto%2C_Japan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/2021_Sagano_Bamboo_forest_in_Arashiyama%2C_Kyoto%2C_Japan.jpg/960px